# TASK F3 — evaluation_core.py (Fable). Owner ONLY new files: conference/model_v2/evaluation_core.py, conference/model_v2/tests/test_evaluation_core.py. No other edits; no job submission; no GPU; no /orcd traversal; no commits; no nested agents. This is a statistics/software-engineering module (data splitting, label-state handling, metric guards, uncertainty) with no wet-lab protocol content.
Read (bounded): conference/model_v2/SCIENTIFIC_LOCK.md; ops/briefs/J9_SMN2_RESULT.md and j9_smn2_prediction.py (existing rank/forbidden-metric guard style, evidence classes); ops/briefs/J6_FIX_RESULT.md (site schema); conference/model_v2/trans_intervention.py (evidence class vocabulary).
## Contract
1) Observation label states (enum, exhaustive): measured_positive, verified_negative, unlabeled, unassayed, censored. Table schema + validator: every row carries label_state, assay/study id, independent_unit_id, and provenance; reject any row that infers verified_negative from absence in a responder-only table (validator requires an explicit negative_evidence field: assayed_and_powered=True with detection limit).
2) Leakage-free grouping: group-aware split generator that keeps together (a) identical/near-identical ASO sequences (Hamming/edit threshold), (b) chemistry family, (c) study, (d) genomically overlapping windows (interval clustering, strand-aware, configurable padding). Modes: leave-one-ASO-out, leave-study-out, region-blocked, nested (outer/inner groups; refuse when independent N is too small and say so). Deterministic with seed; test that no group straddles train/test, that overlapping windows never split, nested inner folds never see outer test groups.
3) Metric guard: AUPRC/AUROC/FDR/accuracy/precision-recall computed ONLY if verified_negative count >= configurable minimum and positives >= minimum; otherwise raise MetricBlocked with reason. Explicit positive-unlabeled mode: report only PU-valid quantities (e.g. rank statistics of positives among unlabeled with a stated class-prior assumption; recall at top-k of the candidate universe) each tagged evidence_class and 'pu_assumption'. Never accept unlabeled as negative.
4) Uncertainty clustered by truly independent units (cluster bootstrap over independent_unit_id; refuse CIs when < min clusters; do not treat correlated windows as independent). Calibration/ties handled; deterministic seeds.
5) Baselines M0 (permuted/random reference), M1..M6 interface: a registry mapping name -> feature column set from the J9/J3 feature table; ablation runner interface (leave-feature-family-out) that returns a typed result with per-fold group ids and blocked-metric reasons. Do not train any model on the July exon-7 gels; add a guard refusing any input file whose path/name matches forbidden outcome sources (SMN2_Exon7_7_27+28_Complete_Data*, psi25/, feng/terminal) .
## Tests (adversarial): leakage traps (duplicate ASO under different ids, overlapping windows across studies, chemistry-family straddle), missingness traps (unassayed treated as negative must raise), tiny-N refusals, deterministic reproducibility, forbidden-source guard, PU-mode never emitting AUPRC.
