   285	                                          min_independent_groups=2)
   286	                except ec.SplitRefused:
   287	                    continue
   288	                assert_no_straddle(plan)
   289	                ec.verify_no_leakage(plan)
   290	                tested = [i for f in plan.folds for i in f.test_idx]

 succeeded in 71ms:
     1	"""F3 - evaluation core: label states, leakage-free splits, guarded metrics, clustered uncertainty.
     2	
     3	Statistics / software-engineering module only. It fits nothing and reads no outcome
     4	data. Five pieces, each refusing loudly instead of degrading silently:
     5	
     6	1. ``validate_table``  - exhaustive label states; a ``verified_negative`` needs explicit
     7	   ``negative_evidence`` (assayed_and_powered is True + finite detection limit) and can
     8	   never come from a responder-only table (absence is not a negative).
     9	2. ``make_splits`` / ``make_nested_splits`` - purged group splits. Four leakage axes:
    10	   near-identical ASO sequence, chemistry family, study, overlapping genomic window.
    11	   The test set is one unit of the mode's primary axis; every other row sharing ANY
    12	   active axis group with a test row is purged (in neither train nor test).
    13	3. ``compute_metric`` - AUROC/AUPRC/FDR/accuracy/precision/recall/calibration only with
    14	   enough verified negatives and positives (counted as independent units), otherwise
    15	   ``MetricBlocked``. ``pu_report`` is the positive-unlabeled alternative and never
    16	   emits a supervised metric. Unlabeled / unassayed / censored are never negatives.
    17	4. ``cluster_bootstrap_ci`` - resamples effective independent clusters
    18	   (``independent_unit_id`` merged with sequence / window overlap); refuses below
    19	   ``min_clusters``.
    20	5. ``BASELINES`` (M0..M6) and ``run_ablation`` (leave-feature-family-out interface).
    21	
    22	``check_source_not_forbidden`` refuses the July exon-7 outcome workbook, any ``psi25``
    23	directory and anything under ``feng/terminal`` (SCIENTIFIC_LOCK).
    24	"""
